#
# The settings a mkfile picks up when it needs a tool that runs on the
# *build* machine rather than on 9front.  On a 9front machine those
# are the same thing and the mkfile says
#
#	eval `{grep '^[A-Z]' $ROOT/9front-src/host/mkfile}
#
# to get them.  Here they are not: 6c makes amd64 9front objects, and
# a generator like libc/ucd's mkrunetype has to run on the host that
# is doing the building.  scripts/import-9front.sh rewrites
# $ROOT/9front-src/host/mkfile to this file, and this file names a host compiler
# that understands Plan 9 C -- plan9port's, which is already required
# for rc.
#
# Only the names a host tool needs are set: CC, LD, O and the flags.
# Nothing here is used to build anything that runs on 9front.
#

# Every line here that starts with a capital is eval'd by the mkfile
# that greps this file, so none of them may have an empty value: rc
# parses "B= C=3" as B being set to the list (C=3), and a 9front
# machine never hits it because its own /$cputype/mkfile has no empty
# assignment either.  Where a flag is not wanted, give one that does
# nothing rather than nothing at all.
CC=$ROOT/9front-src/host/hostcc
LD=$ROOT/9front-src/host/hostld
O=o
CFLAGS=-w
LDFLAGS=-w
